# Cloud Build derives its build context from .gitignore when no
# .gcloudignore is present -- which would silently exclude the pretrained
# model artifacts Dockerfile.predict needs (cache_builder.py loads them via
# NNPredictionService/XGBPredictionService/LRPredictionService), since
# .gitignore excludes models/*.keras and models/*.pkl as large binaries
# that don't belong in git history.
#
# rawdata/ is deliberately NOT re-included here: winspool-predict-daily
# syncs its own copy at job start (see cache_builder.py::_sync_rawdata()),
# since it runs in a separate, stateless Cloud Run Job container from
# winspool-sync-daily with no shared filesystem -- baking a multi-GB
# rawdata/ into the image would be both wasted space and stale by the next
# nflverse update anyway.
#!include:.gitignore

!models/*.keras
!models/*.pkl
